  "output": "\n\nOn it — arming a Lisbon fare watch: SFO→LIS round trip, 5+ day trips departing March–May 2027, pinging you under $500.\n\nThere's already a Lisbon watch spec on file (from Sep 17) but no persisted schedule behind it — so no check is actually firing. Let me create the real job.\n\nThe control-plane schedule route is dead (skill's curl got URL-rejected — no OPENAI_BASE_URL exported), so I'm going through the cron engine directly, same as the other watches on this box:\n\nOne fix — it defaulted to local-only delivery, so the alert wouldn't reach you. Setting it to bot-chat like the other watchers:\n\nDone — Lisbon watch is live. Hourly checks for SFO→LIS round trips under $500, any dates March 1–May 31 2027 with a 5+ day stay; you'll get one ping with airline, dates, and price when it lands, then the watch pauses itself. Heads up: spring fares were sitting around $1,560 when I last looked Sep 17, so a sub-$500 window may take a while — it'll fire the moment one shows up.",
